  "summary": "Correia and Skiles argue that generalized identity can provide a unified analysis of grounding and essence. Full and partial essence are modeled through generic identity and conjunctive parthood, while grounding is modeled through disjunctive parthood and subsumption. The resulting framework aims to explain why grounding implies certain essence-based necessitation patterns without collapsing essence into mere modal equivalence.",
